Concept 1 — Mesh Kya Hota Hai? (From Absolute Zero)
Unity me koi bhi 3D object (wall, cube, character) mesh se bana hota hai.
A Mesh = 3 data lists:

Vertices
→ 3D points (Vector3)
→ Ye actual shape define karte hain

Triangles
→ Vertices ko connect karte hain
→ GPU ko batate hain kaunse 3 points ek surface banate hain

Normals
→ Direction batate hain surface kis side face kar rahi hai
→ Lighting yahin se kaam karti hai

Simple bolu:
Mesh = dots + connections + directions

| fake                     | Reality                         |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------------- |
| Mesh ek solid cheez hai  | Mesh sirf points ka network hai |
| Hole = texture change    | Hole = vertices move            |
| Scale ya cut karna       | Vertex displacement             |
| Physics se apne aap hole | Physics sirf detect karta hai   |


meshFilter.sharedMesh  // ORIGINAL (read-only)
meshFilter.mesh        // CLONE (editable)
Tum kabhi bhi sharedMesh modify nahi karoge.
Always:
Mesh mesh = meshFilter.mesh;
Unity bolega:
"Theek hai, le lo tumhari personal copy."


--> Mesh vertices are ALWAYS in LOCAL SPACE


Example Code 
 MeshFilter mf = GetComponent<MeshFilter>();
Is line me 4 cheezein ho rahi hain. Dhyaan se.
1️⃣ MeshFilter (Type)
MeshFilter Unity ka component hai
Ye batata hai kaunsa mesh render ho raha hai
Har visible 3D object ke paas hota hai:
MeshFilter → shape
MeshRenderer → material
2️⃣ mf (Variable Name)
Ye sirf ek naam hai
Isme hum MeshFilter ka reference store kar rahe hain
Socho:
mf = shortcut naam
3️⃣ GetComponent<MeshFilter>()
Unity se bolo:
“Is GameObject pe jo MeshFilter laga hai, wo mujhe de do”
⚠️ Agar MeshFilter nahi hoga:
mf = null
Next line crash

Why This Line is CRITICAL
Without this:
Mesh access ❌
Vertex access ❌
Deformation ❌
This line is your entry gate into the mesh.

step 2
Mesh mesh = mf.mesh;
1️⃣ Mesh (Type)

Mesh Unity ka object hai

Iske andar hota hai:
vertices
triangles
normals=
bounds
Ye actual geometry data hai.
2️⃣mf.mesh (MOST IMPORTANT PART)
Unity internally ye karta hai:
mf.sharedMesh → ORIGINAL mesh (read-only)
mf.mesh → CLONE bana deta hai (editable)







🧱step 3 
Vector3[] vertices = mesh.vertices;
Vector3[] (Type)
Vector3 = ek point (x, y, z)
Vector3[] = points ki list
Har element = ek vertex
vertices[0] → first point
vertices[1] → second point
...
3️⃣ mesh.vertices
Unity mesh ke saare vertex positions deta hai
Ye positions LOCAL SPACE me hote hain
